
# Project 09 - Advanced Container Runtime Hardening

Secure Internal Web Service Environment

## Project Overview

This project explores advanced container runtime hardening using Docker Compose and an unprivileged NGINX container image.

The project focuses on non-root execution, read-only container filesystems, Linux capability restrictions, temporary filesystem management, process limits and controlled network exposure.

## Technical Objectives

- Deploy a non-root web server container.
- Configure a read-only root filesystem.
- Remove unnecessary Linux capabilities.
- Prevent additional privilege acquisition.
- Configure temporary writable storage.
- Restrict container process creation.
- Apply CPU and memory restrictions.
- Configure controlled network exposure.
- Verify runtime security configurations.
- Validate filesystem write restrictions.

