## Docker Compose Configuration

```yaml
services:
  secureweb:
    image: nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine
    container_name: hardened-web
    user: "101:101"
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:8170:8080"
    cpus: 0.5
    mem_limit: 256m
    pids_limit: 100
    restart: unless-stopped
    privileged: false
    read_only: true
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true
    tmpfs:
      - /tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,nodev,size=64m,mode=1777
    networks:
      - hardened-net
    healthcheck:
      test:
        - CMD
        - wget
        - -q
        - --spider
        - http://127.0.0.1:8080
      interval: 30s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 3
      start_period: 10s

networks:
  hardened-net:
    name: hardened-net
    driver: bridge
```

## Advanced Runtime Security Controls

| Control | Purpose |
|---|---|
| user: 101:101 | Execute the service without root privileges |
| read_only: true | Restrict root filesystem modification |
| cap_drop: ALL | Remove unnecessary Linux capabilities |
| no-new-privileges | Prevent additional privilege acquisition |
| privileged: false | Avoid privileged container execution |
| tmpfs | Provide temporary writable storage |
| noexec | Restrict direct execution from temporary storage |
| nosuid | Disable set-user-ID effects on temporary storage |
| nodev | Prevent device interpretation on temporary storage |
| pids_limit | Restrict container process creation |
| Localhost port binding | Reduce direct external exposure |

## Deployment and Verification

```powershell
docker compose config --quiet
docker compose up -d
docker compose ps
docker stats --no-stream
docker logs hardened-web
docker network inspect hardened-net
```

Web service testing is performed using localhost on port 8170.

## Non-Root Execution Verification

```powershell
docker exec hardened-web id
docker exec hardened-web whoami
docker inspect --format "{{.Config.User}}" hardened-web
```

The configured container user is expected to have a non-zero user identifier.

## Read-Only Filesystem Verification

```powershell
docker inspect --format "{{.HostConfig.ReadonlyRootfs}}" hardened-web
```

Perform a controlled filesystem write test:

```powershell
docker exec hardened-web touch /etc/security-test
```

The write operation is expected to fail because the root filesystem is mounted as read-only.

## Temporary Filesystem Verification

```powershell
docker exec hardened-web touch /tmp/security-test
docker exec hardened-web ls -l /tmp/security-test
docker exec hardened-web rm /tmp/security-test
```

The temporary filesystem permits necessary temporary file operations without making the root filesystem writable.

## Linux Capability Verification

```powershell
docker inspect --format "{{json .HostConfig.CapDrop}}" hardened-web
docker exec hardened-web cat /proc/1/status
```

Review the capability fields within the process status information.

## Privilege and Process Limit Verification

```powershell
docker inspect --format "{{.HostConfig.Privileged}}" hardened-web
docker inspect --format "{{json .HostConfig.SecurityOpt}}" hardened-web
docker inspect --format "{{.HostConfig.PidsLimit}}" hardened-web
```

